WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:02.570
- [Instructor] We're told Alexa
is riding on a Ferris wheel.

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:04.400
Her height above the ground in meters

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.010
is modeled by H of t where
t is the time in seconds.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.670
And we can see that right over here.

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.900
Now what I want to focus on this video

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.900
is some features of this graph.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:16.620
And the features we're gonna focus on,

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:19.790
actually the first of them,
is going to be the midline.

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.810
So pause this video and
see if you can figure out

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:25.450
the midline of this graph, or
the midline of this function.

00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:26.440
And then we're going to think about

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.073
what it actually represents.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.020
Well, Alexia starts off at
five meters above the ground

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:34.590
and then she goes higher,
and higher, and higher,

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.330
and gets as high as 25 meters,

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:39.410
and then goes back as low as
five meters above the ground,

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.030
and as high as 25 meters.

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:43.080
And what we can view the midline as

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:45.890
is the midpoint between these extremes,

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:48.080
or the average of these extremes.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.720
Well, the extremes are
she goes as low as five

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:52.290
and as high as 25.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.540
So what's the average of five and 25?

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:56.120
Well, that would be 15.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:59.430
So the midline would
look something like this.

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:01.950
And I'm actually gonna
keep going off the graph.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:03.840
And the reason is is
to help us think about

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.110
what does that midline even represent.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:09.170
And one way to think about it is

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:13.720
it represents the center of
our rotation in this situation,

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.620
or how high above the ground

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:18.160
is the center of our Ferris wheel?

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:21.060
And to help us visualize that,
let me draw a Ferris wheel.

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:27.023
So I'm going to draw a circle
with this as the center.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:33.520
And so the Ferris wheel would
look something like this.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:39.493
And it has some type of
maybe support structure.

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:45.890
So the Ferris wheel might
look something like that.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:48.623
And this height above the ground,

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:54.720
that is 15 meters, that is what
the midline is representing.

00:01:55.690 --> 00:02:00.690
Now the next feature I want
to explore is the amplitude.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:04.650
Pause this video and think
about what is the amplitude

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.660
of this oscillating
function right over here

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:08.640
and then we'll think about
what does that represent

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:09.670
in the real world,

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:11.920
or where does it come
from in the real world?

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:17.300
Well the amplitude is
the maximum difference

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:20.290
or the maximum magnitude
away from that midline.

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:21.851
And you can see it right over here.

00:02:21.851 --> 00:02:25.690
Actually right when Alexa starts

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:30.690
we have starting 10
meters below the midline,

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.740
10 meters below the center,

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:36.770
and this is when Alexa is right over here.

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:40.210
She is 10 meters below the midline.

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:44.550
And then after, it looks like 10 seconds,

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:46.780
she is right at the midline.

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:49.290
So that means that she is right over here.

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:51.050
Maybe the Ferris wheel is going this way,

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:53.970
at least in my imagination
it's going clockwise.

00:02:53.970 --> 00:02:57.510
And then after another 10
seconds she is at 25 meters.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:01.300
So she is right over there.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:02.190
And you could see that.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:05.140
She is right over there, I
drew that circle intentionally

00:03:05.140 --> 00:03:06.600
of that size.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:10.700
And so we see the
amplitude in full effect.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:14.380
10 meters below to begin the
midline and 10 meters above.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:18.070
And so it's the maximum displacement

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:22.190
or the maximum change from that midline.

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:27.150
And so over here it really
represents the radius

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:30.180
of our Ferris wheel, 10 meters.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:33.450
And then from this part she
starts going back down again.

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:37.100
And then over here she's
back to where she started.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:40.160
Now the last feature I want to explore

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.720
is the notion of a period.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:45.500
What is the period of
this periodic function?

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.383
Pause this video and think about that.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:50.350
Well the period is how
much time does it take

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:51.940
to complete one cycle.

00:03:51.940 --> 00:03:54.010
So here she's starting at the bottom.

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:56.550
And let's see, after 10
seconds, not at the bottom yet.

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:58.180
After 20 seconds, not at the bottom yet.

00:03:58.180 --> 00:03:59.870
After 30 seconds, not at the bottom yet.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:01.980
And then here she is, after 40 seconds,

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:04.940
she's back at the bottom
and about to head up again.

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:09.710
And so this time right
over here, that 40 seconds,

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:11.160
that is the period.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.010
And if you think about
what's going on over here,

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.580
she starts over here five
meters above the ground.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:18.867
After 10 seconds she is right over here,

00:04:18.867 --> 00:04:21.250
and that corresponds to
this point right over here.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:23.200
After 10 more seconds
she's right over there.

00:04:23.200 --> 00:04:24.690
That corresponds to that point.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:26.760
After 10 more seconds she's over here.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.080
That corresponds to that.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.120
And after 10 more seconds,
or total of 40 seconds,

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.540
she's back to where she started.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.770
So the period in this example

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:39.930
shows how long does it take
to complete one full rotation.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:41.350
Now we have to be careful sometimes

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:44.170
when we're trying to
visually inspect the period

00:04:44.170 --> 00:04:45.650
because sometimes it might be tempting

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:47.557
to say, "Start right over here,

00:04:47.557 --> 00:04:49.857
"and say okay, we're 15
meters above the ground.

00:04:49.857 --> 00:04:51.647
"All right, let's see, we're going down.

00:04:51.647 --> 00:04:53.057
"Now we're going up again.

00:04:53.057 --> 00:04:55.257
"And look, we're 15
meters above the ground.

00:04:55.257 --> 00:04:58.090
"Maybe this 20 seconds is a period."

00:04:58.090 --> 00:04:59.710
But when you look at it over here

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:01.530
it's clear that that is not the case.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.790
This point represents this point

00:05:03.790 --> 00:05:05.700
at being 15 meters above the ground,

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:08.800
going down, that's
getting us to this point,

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:11.670
and then after another 10
seconds we get back over here.

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:14.290
Notice, all this is
measuring is half of a cycle

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:15.950
going halfway around.

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.210
In order to go all the way around

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.850
not only do we have to get
to the same exact height,

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:21.790
but we have to be moving
in the same direction.

00:05:21.790 --> 00:05:23.570
We're at 15 meters and going down.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:25.940
Here we're at 15 meters and going up.

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:27.980
So we have to keep going anther 20 seconds

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:32.883
in order to be 15 meters
in the air, and going down.

